  "worked_solution": "Let's add the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ to the plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14255079/assets/1d0703cf1545f9189bcb8fca1b166b6ecbe694421ce6aef8f680387f78d9b048.png)\n\nTo plot the given curve, we follow these steps:\n\n- Start with the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- Then, shift it by $1$ unit **right.**\n\nTherefore, the given graph is $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1).$",
